    "chunk_size_bytes": 1927,
    "chunk_text": "By virtue of the powers vested in the Chairman under Section 57 of National Film Corporation of Sri Lanka Act No 47 of1971 amended by Act No 45 of 1980, powers which have been entertained so far by private distribution circuits, have beencancelled from 18 June 2019 and from that date National Film Corporation of Sri Lanka performs all the functionsincluding scheduling films for cinema halls, releasing films for screening and collecting income from the distribution offilms totally as per the powers of the aforesaid acts.\n\n2. Methodology\n\nDistribution of films within Sri Lanka shall be performed by National Film Corporation of Sri Lanka (Hereinafter referredto as \u201cCorporation\u201d).\n\n2.1 By virtue of the powers vested in the Corporation under the provisions of the Act these regulations arehereby stipulated and all relevant parties should be bound to adhere to all these regulations.\n\n2.2 Method for registration of films\n\n2.2.1 Registration of local films\n\nEvery local film, which is expected to be screened at cinema halls, should be registered properly atthe Corporation.\n\nThe document containing the method for registration of local films is attached herewith. (Annex 01)\n\n2.2.2 Importation of films\n\nRegistered Importers should obtain the written approval of the Chairman of the Corporation(Hereinafter referred to as \u201cChairman\u201d) fulfilling all conditions as per the importation policy issuedby the Corporation to be followed before importation of films.\n\n2.3 Local films registered in the proper manner or films imported will be scheduled by the Corporation for thepurpose of screening.\n\n2.4 Following requirements should be satisfied for the purpose of categorisation and scheduling films.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'07'03PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA 03.07.20193A\n\n2.4.1 Local films"
