    "chunk_text": "2.4.1.5 The films handed over by the producer (Hereinafter referred to as \u201cFilm Reserve\u201d) will beincluded in the Films Reserve to be screened as per the order of dates in the certificate issuedby Public Performance Board.\n\n2.4.1.6 For the purpose of obtaining recommendations for releasing films to Cinema Halls a SchedulingCommittee for local films will be appointed (Hereinafter referred to as \u201cScheduling Committee\u201d).\n\n2.4.2 Imported films\n\n2.4.2.1 Films, which are imported in terms of the importation policy of National Film Corporation,should be handed over to the National Film Corporation by the respective importer.\n\n2.4.2.2 The films, which are handed over in the above manner, will be submitted by Corporation for theapproval of the Public Performance Board.\n\n2.4.2.3 The films, to which the certificate of the Public Performance Board is issued, will be distributedby the Corporation.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'07'03PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA 03.07.20194A\n\n3. The standard charges recovered by Public Performance Board should be borne by the producer/importer of thefilm.\n\n4. With a view to formalize the distribution of films in national films industry, Cinema halls, which at present screenlocal films will be operated as three distribution channels by way of dividing them in to three categories. (Annex06) However for the purpose of screening a special film on the request of producer (Annex 07), Corporation willtake action depending on the situation to appoint maximum number of cinema halls attaching cinema halls in onechannel to another channel on the written approval of the Chairman depending on the recommendations of schedulingcommittee and recommendations made based on the criteria of Evaluation Board."
